    "title": "Cans, Cones, and Round Shapes",
    "subtitle": "How three round solids hide on your kitchen table every day.",
    "body": "Look at a soup can. Its top and bottom are two flat circles, and a curved side wraps around them. This solid is a cylinder. The two circles always match in size.\n\nNow picture an ice-cream cone. It has one flat circle at the bottom, but the side rises up to a single sharp point. We <mark>call this a cone</mark>. So a cone has one circle, while a cylinder has two.\n\nA ball is different again. It has no flat face at all. Every part of its smooth surface curves the same way, so we name it a sphere.\n\nThese three round solids look simple, yet they sit on your table every day.",
